          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\nHistory of Present Illness:  \nThe patient has focal epilepsy of structural etiology, with onset at age 65 years. Seizures are focal to bilateral tonic-clonic and occur at a frequency of one per month. The epilepsy is drug responsive. Brain MRI demonstrates focal cortical dysplasia.\n\nCurrent Antiseizure Medications:  \n- Perampanel  \n- Carbamazepine  \n\nSeizure Burden Summary:  \nOne focal to bilateral tonic-clonic seizure per month.\n\nAssessment:  \nDrug-responsive focal epilepsy with focal to bilateral tonic-clonic seizures, associated with focal cortical dysplasia.\n\nPlan:  \nContinue perampanel and carbamazepine. Continue tracking seizure frequency.\n\nSincerely,  \nEpilepsy Clinic",
